1
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,040
The work is moving.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:05,920
My hands are empty.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,480
For years, programming gave me a quiet confidence:

4
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,600
whatever happens, the craft will feed me.

5
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,500
I know something that people need.

6
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,900
I use AI every day,

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,880
and I see how much it helps me.

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,880
That is exactly why the dependence unsettles me.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,800
More and more, I am a filter

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,400
for what AI produces.

11
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:34,060
I get more done without feeling more capable.

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,660
The direction is still mine.

13
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,500
Writing is something I return to on my own,

14
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,640
without anyone assigning it to me.

15
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,960
I begin with a thought that is not yet clear,

16
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:49,960
and it becomes clearer as I write it down.

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,260
While I write, my hands are not empty.

18
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,400
I do not know what my work

19
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:56,960
will look like in two years.

20
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,100
Until then, I want to keep living,

21
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,840
writing, and trying.
